  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pathways to safety: inclusive, evidence-based response to urgent humanitarian needs in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As Ukraine enters its fifth year of the conflict, 10.8 million people require humanitarian assistance. Ongoing attacks have destroyed over 2.5 million homes and critical infrastructure, leaving millions without shelter and access to essential services. Targeted attacks on Ukraine&apos;s critical infrastructure - especially energy, water, and transport networks - have severely disrupted basic services, deepened vulnerabilities and pose grave protection risks. The objective of this project is to contribute to strengthening the protection of at-risk populations in Ukraine through evidence-based interventions that enhance access to mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS) and veteran reintegration services, focusing on emerging humanitarian needs.</narrative>
  </description>
